.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
This wrapper API encapsulates core \fBp4est\fP data structures and provides functions that clarify the mark-adapt-partition cycle\&. 

There is also an element iterator that can replace the nested loops over trees and tree quadrants, respectively, which can help make application code cleaner\&.
.PP
For most new code, using this API is likely not necessary\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "int p8est_wrap_adapt (\fBp8est_wrap_t\fP * pp)"

.PP
Call p8est_refine, coarsen, and balance to update pp->\fBp8est\fP\&. Checks pp->flags as per-quadrant input against p8est_wrap_flags_t\&. The pp->flags array is updated along with \fBp8est\fP and reset to zeros\&. Creates ghost_aux and mesh_aux to represent the intermediate mesh\&. If zlib is available, the routine checks whether coarsening and balancing the \fBp8est\fP canceled out and skips computing ghost_aux and mesh_aux when possible\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpp\fP The \fBp8est\fP wrapper to work with, must not be hollow\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
boolean whether \fBp8est\fP has changed\&. If true, partition must be called\&. If false, partition must not be called, and complete must not be called either\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_wrap_complete (\fBp8est_wrap_t\fP * pp)"

.PP
Free memory for the intermediate mesh\&. Sets mesh_aux and ghost_aux to NULL\&. This function must be used if both refinement and partition effect changes\&. After this call, we are ready for another mark-refine-partition cycle\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpp\fP The \fBp8est\fP wrapper to work with, must not be hollow\&. 
.RE
.PP

