.SS "\fBp8est_wrap_t\fP* p8est_wrap_new_conn (sc_MPI_Comm mpicomm, \fBp8est_connectivity_t\fP * conn, int initial_level)"

.PP
Create a \fBp8est\fP wrapper from a given connectivity structure\&. The ghost and mesh members are initialized as well as the flags\&. The btype is set to P8EST_CONNECT_FULL\&. This function sets a subset of the wrap creation parameters\&. For full control use \fBp8est_wrap_new_params\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImpicomm\fP We expect sc_MPI_Init to be called already\&. 
.br
\fIconn\fP Connectivity structure\&. Wrap takes ownership\&. 
.br
\fIinitial_level\fP Initial level of uniform refinement\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A fully initialized \fBp8est_wrap\fP structure\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBp8est_wrap_t\fP* p8est_wrap_new_copy (\fBp8est_wrap_t\fP * source, size_t data_size, \fBp8est_replace_t\fP replace_fn, void * user_pointer)"

.PP
Create a \fBp8est\fP wrapper from an existing one\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
This wrapper must be destroyed before the original one\&. We set it to hollow and copy the original \fBp8est\fP data structure\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsource\fP We access the source for debugging purposes\&. 
.br
\fIdata_size\fP The data size installed in the copied forest\&. 
.br
\fIreplace_fn\fP Callback to replace quadrants during refinement, coarsening or balancing in \fBp8est_wrap_adapt\fP\&. May be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIuser_pointer\fP Set the user pointer in \fBp8est_wrap_t\fP\&. Subsequently, we will never access it\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A fully initialized \fBp8est_wrap\fP structure\&. 
.RE
.PP

