.SS "void p8est_wrap_params_init (\fBp8est_wrap_params_t\fP * params)"

.PP
Initialize a default \fBp8est_wrap_params_t\fP structure\&. The parameters are set to create the most basic, hollow wrap structure\&. 
.SS "int p8est_wrap_partition (\fBp8est_wrap_t\fP * pp, int weight_exponent, \fBp4est_locidx_t\fP * unchanged_first, \fBp4est_locidx_t\fP * unchanged_length, \fBp4est_locidx_t\fP * unchanged_old_first)"

.PP
Call p8est_partition for equal leaf distribution\&. Frees the old ghost and mesh first and updates pp->flags along with \fBp8est\fP\&. Creates ghost and mesh to represent the new mesh\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpp\fP The \fBp8est\fP wrapper to work with, must not be hollow\&. 
.br
\fIweight_exponent\fP Integer weight assigned to each leaf according to 2 ** (level * exponent)\&. Passing 0 assigns equal weight to all leaves\&. Passing 1 increases the leaf weight by a factor of two for each level increase\&. CURRENTLY ONLY 0 AND 1 ARE LEGAL VALUES\&. 
.br
\fIunchanged_first\fP If not NULL, is assigned the processor-local index of the first local quadrant that has stayed on this processor\&. If no quadrant has stayed, the value is set to zero\&. This number is in reference to the new (output) partition\&. 
.br
\fIunchanged_length\fP If not NULL, is assigned the number of quadrants that have stayed on this processor\&. If no quadrant has stayed, the value is set to zero\&. 
.br
\fIunchanged_old_first\fP If not NULL, is assigned the processor-local index of the first local quadrant that has stayed with reference to the old (input) partition\&. If no quadrant has stayed, the value is set to zero\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
boolean whether \fBp8est\fP has changed\&. If true, complete must be called\&. If false, complete must not be called\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_wrap_set_coarsen_delay (\fBp8est_wrap_t\fP * pp, int coarsen_delay, int coarsen_affect)"

.PP
Set a parameter that delays coarsening after adaptation\&. If positive each quadrant counts the number of adaptations it has survived\&. Calling this function initializes all quadrant counters to zero\&. On adaptation we only coarsen a quadrant if it is old enough\&. Optionally, we can also delay the time between subsequent coarsenings\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpp\fP A valid \fBp8est_wrap\fP structure\&. 
.br
\fIcoarsen_delay\fP Set how many adaptation cycles a quadrant has to wait to be allowed to coarsen\&. Non-negative number; 0 disables the feature\&. Suggested default value: not larger than 2\&. 
.br
\fIcoarsen_affect\fP Boolean; If true, we not only count from the most recent refinement but also between subsequent coarsenings\&. Suggested default: 0\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_wrap_set_hollow (\fBp8est_wrap_t\fP * pp, int hollow)"

.PP
Change hollow status of the wrap\&. It is legal to set to the current hollow status\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpp\fP The present wrap structure, hollow or not\&. 
.br
\fIhollow\fP The desired hollow status\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_wrap_set_partitioning (\fBp8est_wrap_t\fP * pp, int partition_for_coarsening)"

.PP
Set a parameter that ensures future partitions allow one level of coarsening\&. The partition_for_coarsening parameter is passed to \fBp8est_partition_ext\fP in \fBp8est_wrap_partition\fP\&. If not zero, all future calls to \fBp8est_wrap_partition\fP will partition in a manner that allows one level of coarsening\&. This function does not automatically repartition the mesh, when switching partition_for_coarsening to a non-zero value\&.
.PP
\fBDeprecated\fP
.RS 4
The function will be removed in the future\&. Flags for partitioning can be set using \fBp8est_wrap_new_params\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpp\fP A valid \fBp4est_wrap\fP structure\&. 
.br
\fIpartition_for_coarsening\fP Boolean: If true, all future partitions of the wrap allow one level of coarsening\&. Suggested default: 1\&. 
.RE
.PP

